  "articleBody": "Texas weather can be pretty intense, especially with hail, high winds, and heavy rains. Knowing when to call for a professional post-storm roof inspection is key to protecting your home and avoiding bigger issues later. If you've just experienced a significant storm, even if you don't see obvious damage from the ground, it's a good idea to get it checked out. Hail damage, for instance, isn't always visible to the untrained eye but can lead to leaks and premature roof deterioration. Other signs like missing shingles, dented gutters, or granules in your downspouts are clear indicators. Discounted Roofing Co. specializes in these storm-damage assessments, providing honest guidance on what they find. It’s better to be proactive; early detection can prevent minor damage from becoming a costly roof replacement. Plus, if you're thinking about an insurance claim, getting a professional assessment promptly is crucial for proper documentation.\n\n**When Professional Guidance Helps**\n- **After any significant storm event:** Even if you don't see obvious issues, hidden damage from hail or wind can compromise your roof's integrity.\n- **If you spot missing or displaced shingles:** These are clear signs your roof has been impacted and needs immediate attention to prevent leaks.\n- **When you find granules in gutters or downspouts:** This often indicates the protective layer of your asphalt shingles is wearing away due to impact.\n- **If you notice dents on gutters, vents, or other metal components:** These dents are tell-tale signs of hail impact, suggesting potential roof damage too.\n- **When you see water stains or drips inside your home:** This is an urgent sign of a leak, meaning your roof has already failed to protect your interior.\n- **Before filing an insurance claim:** A professional inspection provides the clear documentation and assessment needed to support your claim effectively.\n\nDon’t wait for a small problem to become a major headache. Our team is experienced in identifying both visible and less obvious storm damage. We provide clear documentation and support through the whole process, especially for insurance claims. \n\nConcerned about recent storm damage? Contact Discounted Roofing Co. for a free roof inspection today.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}